  "worked_solution": "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of a positive and a negative, which gives a negative:\n\n$$\n5\\cdot (-3)=-15\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{5\\cdot (-3)}_{⏟}}_{-15}\\cdot 2=(-15)\\cdot 2.\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that a negative times a positive gives a negative:\n\n$$\n(-15)\\cdot 2=-(15\\cdot 2)=-30\n$$",
